## Issues Encountered

During initial setup, both the Windows and Kali VMs displayed the same IPv4 address because they were both configured with VirtualBox NAT networking. 
This will need to be changed before attack simulation begins so both VMs can communicate on the same private lab network.

## Lessons Learned

During this setup phase, I learned that VirtualBox NAT networking is useful for basic internet access during installation, but it is not the best option for a cybersecurity lab where VMs need to communicate with each other.
For the next phase, I will configure a Host-only Adapter or Internal Network to create a more realistic isolated lab environment.
